Separate-package regeneration where the set name equals the base package it imports.
The destination (wire) is not scanned on the first run, so the injector for set "app"
imports example.com/app and (because the set name reserves "app") aliases that
qualifier to app2. Regenerating with the emitted file now present in the destination
re-scans a package that declares func app; the collision check must drop that
self-introduced declaration rather than fault the set against it, so plumb reproduces
its own output byte-for-byte (asserted by the corpus regeneration pass).
-- config --
import-path: example.com/wire
package-name: wire
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Server struct{}

//plumb:app
func NewServer() *Server { return &Server{} }
